# Activate and Repair A Topology

This Livebook starts a topology with manual repair, stops one member, and asks
the controller to restore the existing target.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define The System

```elixir
defmodule RepairGuide.Cell do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "repair_guide_cell"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{label: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("cell")})
  end
end

defmodule RepairGuide.System do
  use Jido.Topology, name: "repair_guide_system"

  agents do
    agent :left, RepairGuide.Cell do
      initial_state %{label: "left"}
    end

    agent :right, RepairGuide.Cell do
      initial_state %{label: "right"}
    end
  end

  startup do
    concurrency 2
    retry_interval 1_000
    task_timeout 5_000
  end
end
```

## Start With Manual Repair

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
jido = Jido.default_instance()
topology = RepairGuide.System.new!(id: "repair-system", input: %{})

{:ok, controller} =
  Jido.Topology.Controller.start_link(
    jido: jido,
    topology: topology,
    repair: :manual
  )

:ok = Jido.Topology.Controller.await_ready(controller)

left = Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :left)
right = Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :right)

{left, right}
```

## Stop One Member

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(jido, left)

%{
  left_alive?: Jido.AgentServer.alive?(left),
  right_same?: Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :right) == right
}
```

Manual mode retains normal child supervision but does not run a periodic repair
pass.

## Request Repair

```elixir
:ok = Jido.Topology.Controller.reconcile(controller)
:ok = Jido.Topology.Controller.await_ready(controller)

new_left = Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :left)

%{
  restarted?: is_pid(new_left) and new_left != left,
  right_same?: Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :right) == right,
  status: Jido.Topology.Controller.status(controller)
}
```

Healthy members retain their PIDs and state. Repair uses the same topology
target. It does not apply a new definition.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(controller)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Deployment And Shutdown](deployment-and-shutdown.md) for supervision-tree
placement.
